From 20edf19ae30c5666f07fcf3c2b9ddd76c9122cb9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Neo (E2)" <neo@comfort-wiring.dev>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 16:49:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] provider auth: providers sign in with real accounts to
 view shared preferences

  - POST /api/auth/provider/register + /provider/login + GET /provider/me; sessions carry a
    role and /provider/me + the projection route enforce it (patient tokens rejected)
  - shared hardened logout: POST /api/auth/logout revokes any token, always 200
  - ProviderPortal gains a sign-in/create-account gate; the projection lookup now sends the
    provider Bearer token; hardened sign-out clears the token in finally with clear feedback
  - comfort projection route resolves provider identity via app.state.resolve_provider
    (Bearer first; header stub still present, its removal is the next task)
  - tests/provider-auth.api.test.mjs: register/login/me matrix, role enforcement, revocation
  - rides along: aria-pressed on shell option buttons (ENTRY-011 accepted accessibility fix)
